intent: >
  Add proof (portfolio photos) and substance (design principles) to the
  Newport Beach service page — the highest-dwell service area in GA4 — so
  it converts as well as it pulls traffic.

slice: 2/4
kind: feature
behavior_change: additive

reversibility: trivial

scope:
  declared:
    - src/service-areas/newport-beach.njk
  actual:
    - src/service-areas/newport-beach.njk
  drift: []

proof:
  tests_run: "Manual: Chrome via mcp__claude-in-chrome — verified headings, image natural dimensions (1024x768, 1024x576, 1024x768), badge text, blockquote count (zero after honesty fix), and 10 inline cross-links resolve"
  result: green
  failing: 0

tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Static Nunjucks template change. No logic, no state, no data. Verified
    by rendering in dev server and inspecting DOM.

assumptions:
  - "The three portfolio images (poolgarden12.webp, outdoor-fireplace-seating.webp, project3.jpg) are Steve's work and OK to display"
  - "Visitors won't recognize these as portfolio examples from elsewhere on the site (outdoor-fireplace-seating.webp is also on the homepage as 'Luxury Outdoor Living Space' — duplication is fine for showcasing the same work)"
  - "Steve will eventually replace the design-principles copy with his actual voice; current text is a best-guess of what he'd say"

specifications:
  - "Project cards display style descriptors (Mediterranean / Outdoor Living / Hillside) rather than neighborhood names — no false attribution"
  - "Section heading 'Selected Work' (not 'Recent Projects in Newport Beach') signals these are portfolio examples"
  - "Intro copy explicitly says 'representative projects', not Newport Beach specific"
  - "Design principles section replaces invented client testimonials — the standard going forward when real testimonials aren't available"

deviations_from_plan: >
  Plan said 'project cards with TODO Steve markers for neighborhoods'.
  User flagged that as deceitful — pivoted to style-descriptor badges and
  generic-portfolio framing. Same pivot applied to the testimonials block:
  plan said placeholder testimonials with TODO markers; user chose 'reframe
  as design philosophy', so the entire blockquote block was replaced with
  a principles section attributed to Steve. Honesty-driven, not scope creep.

trade_offs: >
  Reusing outdoor-fireplace-seating.webp here AND on the homepage means
  the same image appears twice for visitors who hit both pages. Decided
  the cost is low — different framing, and Steve's portfolio is finite.
  Alternative would have been to leave this card image-less; rejected
  because the visual makes the section.

self_review:
  consistency: >
    Card structure reuses the Services Grid pattern from earlier in the
    file (rounded-lg shadow, grid md:grid-cols-3, p-6/p-8 internal padding).
    Design-principles cards use the same shape as Services Grid.
  metz: N/A — template file, no Ruby.
  honesty: >
    Two passes here. First version had invented neighborhoods on cards
    ("Corona del Mar", "Balboa Peninsula") and invented client quotes
    (Sarah M., David R.). User flagged. Both removed in second pass.
    Worth flagging as a pattern to watch in future content scaffolding.

confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - "src/service-areas/newport-beach.njk:79-108  — three project cards. The portfolio images are real Lytle work; the descriptions are best-guess from visual inspection. Steve should sanity-check the descriptions match the actual projects"
  - "src/service-areas/newport-beach.njk:113-133  — design principles section. The copy is in 'I think this is how Steve would say it' voice — Steve should rewrite to actual voice"
